* text=auto eol=lf

*.blade.php diff=html
*.css diff=css
*.html diff=html
*.md diff=markdown
*.php diff=php

# The CI and the changelog belong to the kit, not to the project that grows out of
# it: they stay out of the distributed package. Everything else (tests, docker, .env.docker)
# ships on purpose — it is working material for whoever installs the kit.
/.github export-ignore
CHANGELOG.md export-ignore
.styleci.yml export-ignore

# `wikis/specs/` is the kit's OWN planning history — 250 files holding the ADRs of the
# features that built the kit itself. It is the same criterion as `.github` above, and the
# same decision `KitUpdate::CAMINHOS_DO_KIT` already makes on the other side: it delivers the
# eleven top-level documents of `wikis/` one by one and never `specs/`. Without this line the
# `create-project` used to hand over what `kit:update` refuses to hand over — and the installed
# project's agent would sweep 250 foreign wikis before writing its first one.
# `wikis/*.md` does NOT go here: the reference wiki is working material for whoever
# installs, and the README treats it as such.
/wikis/specs export-ignore

# `docs/` is the kit's SITE — the documentation that today lives in the READMEs, published on
# GitHub Pages. Same criterion as `/wikis/specs` and `/.github` above: it is kit
# material, not the project that grows out of it. Without this line, every installed
# project would receive dozens of pages about a kit that already became its own code.
# The READMEs do NOT go here: they shrink, but they stay in the dist — they are the
# package's presentation, and it is what Packagist shows.
/docs export-ignore

# `site/` is the site's TOOLCHAIN — the Astro project that generates what `docs/` describes. Same criterion
# as `/docs` above, and the same reason: it is kit material, not the project that grows out of it. Without this
# line, every installed project would receive a documentation `package.json` it never runs,
# next to its own `package.json` — which is exactly what ADR-02 of the site wiki forbids.
/site export-ignore
/site-vitepress export-ignore

# `phpstan.neon`, `phpunit.xml` and `pint.json` do NOT go here: the composer.json `lint`,
# `types:check` and `test` scripts still ship in the dist and without these files
# none of them runs in the installed project. All three are in
# KitUpdate::CAMINHOS_DO_KIT, and tests/Kit/KitUpdateTest.php fails if they come back.
